FreeSDN rebuilds this binary from the pinned module graph in go.mod/go.sum with
its own Go toolchain, then overlays it onto the upstream runtime image. The
upstream runtime contract is preserved; only the compiled binary is replaced.

The rebuild exists because the published image is compiled with an older Go
toolchain. On 2026-10-09 the current upstream release carried two fixable HIGH
Go standard-library advisories, CVE-2026-78667 and CVE-2026-97031, both fixed in
Go 1.26.9 and 1.27.2. It was the only one of the fifteen release components not
built from source, and the only one with fixable findings.
